{
"dur": 37.766,
"shots": [
{
"i": 1,
"start": 0.0,
"vo_start": 0.6,
"vo_end": 6.158,
"text": "A man who washed dishes at Denny's as a teenager now runs the first company in history worth five trillion dollars.",
"end": 6.433
},
{
"i": 2,
"start": 6.433,
"vo_start": 6.708,
"vo_end": 14.521,
"text": "It started in 1993, in a booth at a Denny's in San Jose, where three engineers drank refill coffee and argued about a chip that didn't exist yet.",
"end": 14.796
},
{
"i": 3,
"start": 14.796,
"vo_start": 15.071,
"vo_end": 21.083,
"text": "Within a few years, their company built the wrong chip, lost almost everything, and came within about a month of running out of money.",
"end": 21.358
},
{
"i": 4,
"start": 21.358,
"vo_start": 21.633,
"vo_end": 28.374,
"text": "The chip that nearly killed it is the reason it won. And the bet that made it a giant earned almost nothing for six years.",
"end": 28.649
},
{
"i": 5,
"start": 28.649,
"vo_start": 28.924,
"vo_end": 36.816,
"text": "This is the story of Nvidia, and of Jensen Huang, a man who later said his will to survive exceeded almost everybody else's will to kill him.",
"end": 37.766
}
],
